p.src:
We can make the arithmetic explicit in a way the lecture itself only implies: $\begin{aligned}
\text{do nothing}
&\Longrightarrow
5 \text{ deaths},\\
\text{kill }1\text{ healthy man and distribute the organs}
&\Longrightarrow
1 \text{ death and }5 \text{ survivals},\\
\Delta N_{\text{lives}}
&=
5 - 1 = 4.\end{aligned}$ The notation is editorial, but the structure is faithful. If each life is counted symmetrically, the second act seems to improve the total outcome.

